{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added per-feed `fetch_timeout` (integer seconds, 0 = use global timeout).\n\n- Model: `Feed.FetchTimeout` (`json:\"fetch_timeout\"`), `FeedModificationRequest.FetchTimeout` (*int) applied in `Patch`, and a `Feed.HTTPClientTimeout()` helper that returns the per-feed value when > 0, otherwise the global `HTTP_CLIENT_TIMEOUT`.\n- Database: new migration adds `feeds.fetch_timeout int not null default 0`.\n- Storage: `UpdateFeed` writes the column; the feed query builder reads it, so it appears in the API feed object.\n- Fetching: feed refresh, entry processing/scraping and the icon checker now use the feed's timeout instead of the global one.\n- Validation: `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}` rejects a negative `fetch_timeout`. The error message is a plain English string, not a translated locale key.\n- Go client: `fetch_timeout` added to `Feed` and `FeedModificationRequest`.\n\nNot done: the field is not settable at feed creation, not in the web UI edit form, and not in OPML import/export. First-time subscription fetches still use the global timeout.\n\nExisting unit and integration tests pass; the new behaviour itself (a slow server timing out at the per-feed value) was not exercised by any test I ran.", "t": 1794463067.698}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794463067.698}
